hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5597","I wrote this and sent it to Umar bin Abdul Aziz during his caliphate, so he wrote a letter to Abu Bakr bin Muhammad to inquire from Muhammad bin Thabit about the narrations he transmitted, because he is a trustworthy narrator. Abu Bakr bin Muhammad inquired from him about this, then wrote to Umar bin Abdul Aziz, so Umar bin Abdul Aziz imposed a ban on women entering the bathhouse."
"5598","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""A woman is an object of concealment; when she goes out, Satan looks at her, and she is closest to Allah the Exalted when she is in the innermost part of her house."
"5599","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""A woman is an object of concealment; when she goes out, Satan looks at her. A woman is closest to her Lord when she is in the innermost part of her house."
"5600","I have felt death even before tasting it, and a coward dies a natural death. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) inquired about the condition of Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), and he replied: ""Alas! Will I ever spend a night on a path where around me will be Idhkhir and Jalil (specific grasses of Makkah)?"" Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) went to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and informed him about the responses of these individuals. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) raised his gaze towards the sky and made this supplication: ""O Allah, make Madinah Munawwarah as beloved to us as You made Makkah beloved to us, or even more intensely beloved. O Allah! Bless us in its Sa’ and its Mudd, and transfer its disease to Mahya’ah."" (The narrator states) By this is meant Juhfah."
"5601","The Shaykh explains: The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Women do not have the right to walk in the road,"" is literally an informative statement, but the real intent is to prohibit what is implied within it, and that is that women should not walk alongside men, because generally men walk in the middle of the road, so it is necessary for women to walk separately on the sides of the road so that they can avoid mingling with men."
"5602","Umm Salamah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permission for getting herself cupped. He commanded Abu Tibah to cup her. The transmitter said: I think he was her foster-brother or a boy not yet of age. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4105)"
"5603","The narrators named Umar, Ya'la, and Muhammad are all sons of Ubaid Tanafi; they are residents of Kufa and are trustworthy."
"5604","When any one of you fights with his brother he should avoid striking at the face. (Using translation from Muslim 2612a)"
"5605","narrates that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""When a person beats (another), he should avoid the face, because Allah Almighty created Sayyiduna Adam, peace be upon him, in His image."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) What is meant by this is: the person who is being beaten, his appearance is (in accordance with) the image of Sayyiduna Adam, peace be upon him, because when the one who beats strikes the face of his Muslim brother, Allah Almighty created Sayyiduna Adam, peace be upon him, in his image."
"5606","""Some people apostatized after accepting Islam, and 'Ali burned them with fire. Ibn 'Abbas said: 'If it had been me, I would not have burned them; the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'No one should be punished with the punishment of Allah.' If it had been me, I would have killed them; the Messenger of Allah [SAW] said: 'Whoever changes his religion, kill him.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4060)"
"5607","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever shoots an arrow at us is not one of us."
"5608","Do not make anything having life as a target. (Using translation from Muslim 1957a)"
"5609","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up an animal (and then shooting at it as a target)."
"5610","We fought along with AbdurRahman ibn Khalid ibn al-Walid. Four infidels from the enemy were brought to him. He commanded about them and they were killed in confinement. Abu Dawud said: The narrators other than Sa'id reported from Ibn Wahb in this tradition: ""(killed him) with arrows in confinement."" When Abu Ayyub al-Ansari was informed about it, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibiting to kill in confinement. By Him in Whose hands my soul is, if there were a hen, I would not kill it in confinement. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Khalid b. al-Walid was informed about it (the Prophet's prohibition). He set four slaves free. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2687)"
"5611","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""When you encounter Ahbar bin Aswad and Nafi’ bin ‘Abd Qais, burn both of them in the fire."" After this, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Only Allah Almighty can punish with fire. When you encounter both of them, then kill them."
"5612","‘Urwa bin Al Zubair said “Hisham bin Halim bin Hizam found a man who was the governor of Hims making some Copts stand in the sun for the payment of jizyah. He said “What is this?” I heard the Apostle ﷺ as saying “Allaah Most High will punish those who punish the people in this world.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3045)"
"5613","‘Urwa bin Al Zubair said “Hisham bin Halim bin Hizam found a man who was the governor of Hims making some Copts stand in the sun for the payment of jizyah. He said “What is this?” I heard the Apostle ﷺ as saying “Allaah Most High will punish those who punish the people in this world.” (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3045)"
"5614","An ant stung a prophet. He ordered a colony of ants to be burned. Allah revealed to him : because an ant stung you, you have perished a community which glorifies Me. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5266)"
"5615","The narrator says: I replied: Yes. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Whatever Allah grants you is lawful. Allah’s wrist is stronger than your wrist, and Allah’s razor is sharper than your razor. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The words of the narration: “Allah’s wrist is stronger than your wrist,” are according to the idiom of the people, because the meaning can only be conveyed to the listener according to their idiom. The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): “Everything that Allah has given you is lawful for you,” here, literally, is in the imperative form, but what is meant by it is to prohibit that thing because of this practice, and that is the people’s behavior regarding camels: they cut their ears and slit their skins, then declare them forbidden for themselves."
"5616","I have vowed that if I find him, I will surely cut off his hand. Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Do not cut off his hand. Once, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us (to deliver a sermon), and he commanded us to give charity and forbade mutilation."
"5617","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Allah Almighty has cursed the person who mutilates an animal."
"5618","I (had the honour of) leading the white mule on which rode Allah's Apostle ﷺ and with him were Hasan and Husain, till it reached the apartment of Allah's Apostle ﷺ. The one amongst them was seated before him and the other one was seated behind him. (Using translation from Muslim 2423)"
"5619","narrates from his father, who was a companion of the Prophet (peace be upon him), that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Ride these animals with safety, and do not make them chairs.” (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This means do not use them in such a way that you never get down from them."
"5620","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the person who had done this, then he said: ""Subhan Allah! Do not strike them on their faces."
"5621","“A woman entered Hell because of a cat which she tied up and did not feed, or let it loose to eat of the vermin of the earth, until it died.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4256)"
"5622","I wished, I could have taken a bunch from it. Hell was also presented before me; if I had not pushed it away, it would have engulfed you. I saw three people in it who were being punished. One was a tall, dark-skinned woman from Yemen who was being punished because of a cat. She had tied up the cat. She did not let it go so it could eat on its own, nor did she give it anything to eat, until the cat died. Then the cat would come to her, then come from behind her, and scratch her. (I saw in Hell) a man from Banu Dada’ah who had an issue with two she-camels, who was tied between two pillars in Hell. (The narrator says) those two she-camels were among the sacrificial animals of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which that man had stolen. (The Prophet said) I saw a man with a stick, who was leaning on his stick. This man used to steal the belongings of pilgrims with his stick; when his theft remained hidden, he would take the goods away, and when he was caught, he would say: I did not steal; this thing just got caught on my stick."
"5623","I will always brand on the back part of its body. Then Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) branded it on its ja'irah (the part of the thigh where the animal's tail reaches when it wags)."
"5624","By Allah, I do not cauterise (the animal) but on a part at a distance from the face, and commanded (for the cauterisation) of his ass and it was cauterised on the buttocks and he was the first to cauterise on the buttocks. (Using translation from Muslim 2118)"
"5625","By Allah, I do not cauterise (the animal) but on a part at a distance from the face, and commanded (for the cauterisation) of his ass and it was cauterised on the buttocks and he was the first to cauterise on the buttocks. (Using translation from Muslim 2118)"
"5626","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: May Allah curse the person who did this. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade branding on the face and hitting on the face."
"5627","I not forbid this? May Allah curse the one who did this."
"5628","Allah has cursed one who has cauterised it (on the face). (Using translation from Muslim 2117)"
"5629","The narrator named Shu’bah says: I am fairly certain that the narration also contains these words: You were branding their ears."
"5630","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever kills a snake will receive seven good deeds, and whoever kills a lizard will receive one good deed."
"5631","“O Mother of the Believers, what do you do with this?” She said: “We kill these house lizards with it, for the Prophet of Allah ﷺ told us that when Ibrahim was thrown into the fire, there was no beast on earth that did not try to put it out, apart from the house lizard that blew on it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that they should be killed.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3231)"
"5632","Abu Hurairah reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying There are five(creatures) the killing of which is lawful in the sacred territory. The Snake, the Scorpion, the Kite, the Rat and the biting Dog. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1847)"
"5633","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'There are five kinds of vermin that may be killed in the Haram: Scorpions, mice, crows, vicious dogs, and kites."" (Sahih) Chaper 120. The Prohibition Of Disturbing The Game Of The Haram (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2891)"
"5634","narrates: She asked the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) about killing a lizard, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ordered it to be killed."
"5635","The Messenger of Allah (May peace be upon him) ordered a gecko to be killed, and calling it a noxious little creature. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5262)"
"5636","""Geckos are vermin."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2886)"
"5637","I found him saying his prayer, so I sat down waiting for him to finish his prayer when I heard a stir in the bundles (of wood) lying in a comer of the house. I looked towards it and found a snake. I jumped up in order to kill it, but he (Abu Sa'id Khudri) made a gesture that I should sit down. So I sat down and as he finished (the prayer) he pointed to a room in the house and said: Do you see this room? I said: Yes. He said: There was a young man amongst us who had been newly wedded. We went with Messenger of Allah ﷺ (to participate in the Battle) of Trench when a young man in the midday used to seek permission from Messenger of Allah ﷺ to return to his family. One day he sought permission from him and Messenger of Allah ﷺ (after granting him the permission) said to him: Carry your weapons with you for I fear the tribe of Quraiza (may harm you). The man carried the weapons and then came back and found his wife standing between the two doors. He bent towards her smitten by jealousy and made a dash towards her with a spear in order to stab her. She said: Keep your spear away and enter the house until you see that which has made me come out. He entered and found a big snake coiled on the bedding. He darted with the spear and pierced it and then went out having fixed it in the house, but the snake quivered and attacked him and no one knew which of them died first, the snake or the young man. We came to Allah's Apostle ﷺ and made a mention to him and said: Supplicate to Allah that that (man) may be brought back to life. Thereupon he said: Ask forgiveness for your companion and then said: There are in Medina jinns who have accepted Islam, so when you see any one of them, pronounce a warning to it for three days, and if they appear before you after that, then kill it for that is a devil. (Using translation from Muslim 2236a)"
"5638","“Kill snakes, and kill Dhit-Tufytain* and the Abtar, for they take away the sight and cause miscarriage.” *A snake that has two white stripes on its back. A snake with a short or mutilated tail. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3535)"
"5639","narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Lubabah (may Allah be pleased with him) has stated that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded to kill the snakes present in the houses."
"5640","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Snakes are a deformed form of jinn, just as pigs and monkeys are deformed (creatures)."
"5641","The narrator named Muhammad bin Abu Yahya is the father of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Abu Yahya, who was a student of Imam Shafi'i."
"5642","“Kill snakes, and kill Dhit-Tufytain* and the Abtar, for they take away the sight and cause miscarriage.” *A snake that has two white stripes on its back. A snake with a short or mutilated tail. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3535)"
"5643","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded to kill them. Both of them said: The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has forbidden killing snakes that come out in houses."
"5644","The narrator says: The Prophet said this regarding snakes.) And whoever refrains from killing any one of them out of fear is not from among us."
"5645","Kill snakes, kill those which have two streaks and those with small tails, for they obliterate the eyesight and cause miscarriage. Salim said: ‘Abd Allah(b. ‘Umar) used to kill every snake which he found. Abu Lubabah or Zaid b. al-Khattab saw him chasing a snake. He said: He(the Prophet) prohibited house-snakes. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5252)"
"5646","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing shrikes*, frogs, ants and hoopoes.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3223)"
"5647","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). However, in that narration, these words are present: ""These ants used to glorify Allah."
"5648","the Messenger of Allah commanded that dogs be killed, except those which were exempted. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4277)"
"5649","Messenger of Allah, I find a change in your mood today. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Gabriel had promised me that he would meet me tonight, but he did not meet me. By Allah, he never broke his promises, and Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the day in this sad (mood). Then it occurred to him that there had been a puppy under their cot. He commanded and it was turned out. He then took some water in his hand and sprinkled it at that place. When it was evening Gabriel met him and he said to him: you promised me that you would meet me the previous night. He said: Yes, but we do not enter a house in which there is a dog or a picture. Then on that very morning he commanded the killing of the dogs until he announced that the dog kept for the orchards should also be killed, but he spared the dog meant for the protection of extensive fields (or big gardens). (Using translation from Muslim 2105)"
"5650","""Whoever keeps a dog. Except a dog for hunting or herding livestock, two Qirats will be deducted from his reward each day."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4287)"
"5651","The Prophet of Allah ﷺ ordered to kill dogs, and we were even killing a dog which a woman brought with her from the desert. Afterwards he forbade to kill them, saying: Confine yourselves to the type which is black. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2846)"
"5652","He who kept a dog would lose out of his deeds equal to one qirat every day. except (one kept) for watching the field or herd. (Using translation from Muslim 1575c)"
"5653","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog, except for the purpose of guarding crops or livestock, two qirats are deducted from his reward every day."
"5654","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever keeps a dog, one Qirat will be deducted from him (good) deeds every day, except a dog for farming or herding livestock.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3204)"
"5655","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever keeps a dog that is not for hunting, or for guarding crops, or for guarding livestock, then a qirat (portion) of their reward is reduced every day."
"5656","The name of the narrator called Abu Sufyan is Saad, and his title is ""Sils."" There is no other musnad hadith in the world narrated from Abu Sufyan bin Alaa except this one. He was the brother of Abu Amr bin Alaa, and Amr bin Alaa's name was Zaban. They were four brothers. (The names of the other two brothers) are Abu Muadh and Umar."
"5657","""Were it not that dogs form one of the communities (or nations - of creatures), I would have commanded that they be killed. But kill those that are all black. Any people who keep a dog, except for dogs used for farming, hunting or herding livestock, one Qirat will be deducted from their reward each day."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4280)"
"5658","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""If dogs were not a specific type of creature, I would have ordered them to be killed. However, kill the black dog among them, for it is a devil."
"5659","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted keeping a dog for (the protection of) fields."
"5660","Do not hate each other; do not envy each other; do not desert each other; and be the servants of Allah as brethren. It is not allowed for a Muslim to keep apart from his brother for more than three days. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4910)"
"5661","The gates of Paradise are opened every Monday and Thursday, and Allah forgives every servant who does not associate anything with Allah, except for the person who has enmity with his brother. It is said regarding them: 'Keep checking on both of them until they reconcile.' (Their forgiveness will not be granted.) 'Keep checking on both of them until they reconcile.' (Their forgiveness will not be granted.)"
"5662","The conduct you have adopted, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade it. It is not permissible for any Muslim to remain estranged from his brother for more than three days.” When both of them admonished and advised Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) at length, she began to remind them and started to weep, saying: “I have made a vow, and the matter of a vow is severe.” But both of them continued to speak with her until Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) began to converse with ‘Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both). Then Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) freed forty slaves as expiation for her vow. Even after freeing forty slaves, she would continue to weep until her shawl would become wet with her tears. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) was the maternal aunt of ‘Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both), because the mother of ‘Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with them both), Lady Asma’ bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both), was the sister of Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)."
"5663","""The gates of Paradise are opened on Monday and Thursday. In them, (will enter) whoever has not associated anything with Allah will be forgiven, except for the two who shun each other, (about whom) it is said: 'Return these two until they make amends."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2023)"
"5664","The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “They will not enter Paradise, nor will they be together in Paradise,” means: If Allah, the Exalted, does not forgive them for their estrangement out of His grace, (then they will not enter Paradise)."
"5665","from the Prophet ﷺ who said, *""Allah ˹audits˺ His creation on the middle night of Shaʿbān and He forgives all of His creation, except for an idolater or one filled with malice.""*"
"5666","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On Mondays and Thursdays, the gates of Paradise are opened, and Allah forgives every Muslim servant who does not associate anything with Allah, except for the person who has enmity with his brother. It is said: Defer the matter of these two until they reconcile, defer the matter of these two until they reconcile."
"5667","Leave them and put them off until they are turned to reconciliation. (Using translation from Muslim 2565d)"
"5668","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""On Mondays and Thursdays, the gates of Paradise are opened, and every Muslim servant who does not associate anything with Allah is forgiven, except for the person who is harboring enmity with his brother. It is commanded regarding them: Delay their matter until they reconcile."
"5669","it is not allowable for a Muslim to keep apart from his brother for more than three days. When they meet, this turns away from him, and that turns away from him. The better of the two is the one who initiates in salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4911)"
"5670","it is not allowable for a Muslim to keep apart from his brother for more than three days. When they meet, this turns away from him, and that turns away from him. The better of the two is the one who initiates in salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4911)"
"5671","The Prophet ﷺ said: Allah Most High says: Pride is my cloak and majesty is my lower garment, and I shall throw him who view with me regarding one of them into Hell. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4090)"
"5672","I will admit him into Hell."
"5673","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to sit on his knees; he did not lean back."
"5674","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Are you sitting in this manner? The way those people sit upon whom wrath has been sent down. Ibn Jurayj has narrated these words: They had placed their palms on the ground behind their backs."
"5675","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she was asked: What work did the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) do at home? Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied: He used to wash his clothes like an ordinary person, milk his goat, and do his own work himself."
"5676","The same as any one of you does in his household chores. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would mend his own sandals, sew his own clothes, and repair his own bucket."
"5677","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she was asked: What work did the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) do at home? She replied: He used to sew his own clothes, mend his own shoes, and did all those tasks that men do in their homes."
"5678","The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever adopts humility for the sake of Allah by one degree,"" by this he means whoever adopts humility with the creation for the sake of attaining Allah's pleasure; thus, the word ""creation"" is omitted here. The statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever shows arrogance,"" by this he means whoever deals arrogantly with Allah's creation; here too, the word ""creation"" is omitted, because whoever shows arrogance against Allah becomes a disbeliever."
"5679","Sayyiduna Haritha bin Wahb Khuzai (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: \""Shall I not guide you to the people of Paradise? Every weak and poor person (is among the people of Paradise); if he swears by Allah's name, Allah fulfills it for him. And every arrogant and harsh-tempered person is among the people of Hell.\"""""""
"5680","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""A person who has even a mustard seed's weight of arrogance in his heart will not enter Paradise, and a person who has even a mustard seed's weight of faith in his heart will not enter Hell.\""(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration can have two meanings. One of them is what we have mentioned in one category: then, such a person will not enter Paradise who has"
"5681","“Whoever lets his garment drag out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3569)"
"5682","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) disliked wearing the lower garment below the ankles, women displaying their adornment to anyone other than their husbands, intercourse with a woman in her back passage, playing with dice, wearing a ring of brass (or using yellow color), changing the color of the hair, hanging amulets, and performing incantations; however, the ruling regarding the Mu'awwidhat (i.e., the two chapters of seeking refuge or supplicatory prayers for protection) is different."
"5683","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) declared ten things as disliked: changing the color of white (hair), wearing a gold ring, playing with dice, performing ruqyah (incantations), hanging amulets, letting the lower garment hang (below the ankles), yellow (color), displaying adornment unlawfully, and removing water (i.e., semen) from its designated place (all these actions were declared disliked)."
"5684","I would not narrate any hadith to you people. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ‘Among those before you, there was a man who was walking arrogantly; his hair and his garments had made him conceited. Allah Almighty caused the earth to swallow him up, and he will continue to sink in it until the Day of Resurrection.’”"
"5685","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever makes a picture will be punished by being told to put a soul into it, and he will not be able to put a soul into it. And whoever narrates a false dream will be made to tie two grains of barley together, and he will be punished for that. And whoever listens to people's conversations secretly while they dislike it, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection."
"5686","If anyone makes a representation of anything, Allah will punish him on the Day of Resurrection for it until he breathes into it, but he will be unable to do so. If anyone pretends to have had a dream which he did not see, he will be ordered to tie a knot in a grain of barley. If anyone listens to other people’s talk when they try to avoid him, lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 5024)"
"5687","Avoid suspicion, for suspicion is the gravest lie in talk and do not be inquisitive about one another and do not spy upon one another and do not feel envy with the other, and nurse no malice, and nurse no aversion and hostility against one another. And be fellow-brothers and servants of Allah. (Using translation from Muslim 2563a)"
"5688","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: When one of you becomes angry while standing, he should sit down. If the anger leaves him, well and good; otherwise he should lie down. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4782)"
"5689","Sayyiduna Jariyah bin Qudamah (may Allah be pleased with him): He submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah, tell me someth"
"5690","Sayyiduna Jariyah bin Qudamah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A man presented himself before the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and said, ""Please advise me, and grant me a brief advice."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not get angry."" That man asked you the same question again, so you said the same: ""Do not get angry."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""Do not get angry,"" by this he meant: After becoming angry, do not do anything from which I have forbidden you. It does not mean that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) has prohibited feeling anger, because anger is part of human nature, and it is impossible to prohibit a person from something that is inherent in his nature. Rather, this prohibition is regarding those actions that result from anger, as we have mentioned."
"5691","I replied: That a person overpowers others. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Overpowering (or strength) is that a person controls himself at the time of anger."
"5692","Two men abused each other in front of the Prophet ﷺ while we were sitting with him. One of the two abused his companion furiously and his face became red. The Prophet ﷺ said, ""I know a word (sentence) the saying of which will cause him to relax if this man says it. Only if he said, ""I seek refuge with Allah from Satan, the outcast.' "" So they said to that (furious) man, 'Don't you hear what the Prophet ﷺ is saying?"" He said, ""I am not mad."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6115)"
"5693","""Nothing is heavier on the believer's Scale on the Day of Judgment than good character. For indeed Allah, Most High, is angered by the shameless obscene person."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2002)"
"5694","I love the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."" Marwan said something bad to him and then turned away and left. Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) finished his prayer and said, ""You have hurt me. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Indeed, Allah dislikes the one who uses obscene language and foul speech.' And you are one who uses obscene language and foul speech."
"5695","""Nothing is heavier on the believer's Scale on the Day of Judgment than good character. For indeed Allah, Most High, is angered by the shameless obscene person."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2002)"
"5696","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her)! The worst among people is the one whom people avoid because of his bad language."
"5697","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The most hated person in the sight of Allah is the most quarrelsome person."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2457)"
"5698","“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, tell me of something that I can adhere to.’ He said: ‘Say: “Allah is my Lord,” then stand straight (adhere steadfastly to Islam).’ He said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that you fear most for me?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his own tongue, then he said: ‘This.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3972)"
"5699","I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Inform me about a matter that I may hold fast to."" He said: 'Say: My Lord is Allah, then be steadfast.' I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you fear most for me?"" So he took hold of his tongue and said: 'This.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2410)"
"5700","“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, tell me of something that I can adhere to.’ He said: ‘Say: “Allah is my Lord,” then stand straight (adhere steadfastly to Islam).’ He said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that you fear most for me?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his own tongue, then he said: ‘This.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3972)"
"5701","I guarantee Paradise for him.”"
"5702","“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, tell me of something that I can adhere to.’ He said: ‘Say: “Allah is my Lord,” then stand straight (adhere steadfastly to Islam).’ He said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that you fear most for me?’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of his own tongue, then he said: ‘This.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3972)"
"5703","""For whomever Allah protects against the evil of what is between his jaws and the evil of what is between his legs, he shall enter Paradise."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2409)"
"5704","“Modesty is part of faith, and faith will be in Paradise. Obscenity in speech is part of harshness and harshness will be in Hell.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4184)"
"5705","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: If anyone swears on oath is the course which he says: ""By al-Lat"" he should say: There is no god but Allah, and that if anyone says to his friend: Come and let me play for money with you, he should give something in charity (sadaqah). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3247)"
"5706","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""A man utters a word, regarding which he perceives no harm, but because of that word he will keep falling into Hell for seventy years."
"5707","The servant speaks words for which he is sent down to the Hell-Fire farther than the distance between the east and the west. (Using translation from Muslim 2988a)"
"5708","The servant speaks words for which he is sent down to the Hell-Fire farther than the distance between the east and the west. (Using translation from Muslim 2988a)"
"5709","The Prophet Muhammad called a person by his title. The Prophet was informed, ""O Messenger of Allah ( )! This person dislikes it."" So Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""Do not call each other by bad names. After believing, calling someone a sinner is a bad name."" The narrator states: It was the practice of the Ansar that whoever Allah willed, they would give charity and donations, until once a famine struck them, so they stopped doing so. Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw yourselves into destruction with your own hands, and do good; indeed, Allah loves those who do good."",""He (the Prophet) said"",""'The Ansar used to give in charity and provide whatever Allah willed"","" until difficulties befell them. So they refrained from doing so. Then Allah revealed"","" 'And spend in the way of Allah and do not throw [yourselves] with your [own] hands into destruction [by refraining]. And do good; indeed"","" Allah loves the doers of good.'"""""""""
"5710","narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""No person should ever say, 'May Allah disfigure your face and the face that resembles your face,' because Allah the Exalted created Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) in His own image."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) What is meant here is the appearance of the person to whom it was said: 'May Allah disfigure your face,' who is from the offspring of Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him). And the evidence that the address here is to the children of Adam and not to anyone else is the statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""And the face that resembles your face,"" because the face of Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) resembles the appearance of his children."
